VulkanFluid
  build.c                    static C++17 library
  fld/fld.hpp                public API
  fld/core/                  particle state and GPU simulation
  fld/material/              SI material properties
  fld/render/                tile bins and liquid compositor
  fld/shaders/               SPIR-V compute kernels
  research.md                algorithms and validation contract

Current implementation: first GPU baseline, not the completed research paper.
  GPU-resident particles, spatial-hash neighbor graph, PBF pressure projection,
  bounded capillary surface-force approximation, contact-line friction,
  GPU screen-space tile lists and density-isosurface optical rendering.
  This does NOT reproduce the full unified implicit Probst-Teschner solver.
  Neither full Vulkan C++ compilation nor 60 FPS on M2 has been measured.

VulkanEngine must be initialized before fld::system::init.
  fld::system::init(options,initial_drop,shader_paths);
  fld::render::init(renderer_shader_paths,frames,width,height);
  fld::system::record(command,elapsed_seconds);
  fld::render::record(command,frame,targets);
  fld::render::shutdown();
  fld::system::shutdown();

All units are SI. The game supplies liquid material, drop radius/position,
floor height and shaders. The generic library never names blood, characters,
weapons, or gameplay rules.

Validation:
  GitHub Actions gpu-fluid.yml compiles and validates all 12 SPIR-V stages.
  Physical SI helpers have headless deterministic unit tests.
  Full C++ compilation, GPU timing, conservation and capillary benchmarks
  still require a VulkanEngine-enabled machine.
